Find the hypotenuse $h$ of this right-angled triangle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0); \coordinate (B) at (0,2.1); \coordinate (C) at (2.8,0);
\draw[black] (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw[black] (0,0.2)--(0.2,0.2)--(0.2,0);
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,left] {$15\text{ cm}$};
\path (A)--(C) node[midway,below] {$20\text{ cm}$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,above right] {$h$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the hypotenuse $x$. Leave your answer in exact form.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0); \coordinate (B) at (0,1.6); \coordinate (C) at (2.8,0);
\draw[black] (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw[black] (0,0.2)--(0.2,0.2)--(0.2,0);
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,left] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\path (A)--(C) node[midway,below] {$7\text{ cm}$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,above right] {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A rectangular gate is $2.6\text{ m}$ wide and $1.5\text{ m}$ high. Find the length of its diagonal brace $d$, correct to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0); \coordinate (B) at (0,1.5); \coordinate (C) at (2.6,0); \coordinate (D) at (2.6,1.5);
\draw[black] (A)--(B)--(D)--(C)--cycle;
\draw[black] (B)--(C);
\draw[black] (0,0.2)--(0.2,0.2)--(0.2,0);
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,left] {$1.5\text{ m}$};
\path (A)--(C) node[midway,below] {$2.6\text{ m}$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,above right] {$d$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

One shorter side is given as a surd. Find the hypotenuse $x$ in exact form.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0); \coordinate (B) at (0,2.1); \coordinate (C) at (2.5,0);
\draw[black] (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw[black] (0,0.2)--(0.2,0.2)--(0.2,0);
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,left] {$3\text{ cm}$};
\path (A)--(C) node[midway,below] {$\sqrt{13}\text{ cm}$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,above right] {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Jayden calculates the hypotenuse and writes $x^2=9^2+40^2=1681$, then concludes $x=1681\text{ cm}$. Explain his mistake and give the correct length.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0); \coordinate (B) at (0,0.9); \coordinate (C) at (4,0);
\draw[black] (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw[black] (0,0.15)--(0.15,0.15)--(0.15,0);
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,left] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\path (A)--(C) node[midway,below] {$40\text{ cm}$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,above right] {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
